  "description": "The openers' markers (#791, O1): an Outbox that hands out seqs writes a marker of its own into meta in one synced commit when it opens (or, opened with arm false as the quarantine command opens it, before its first batch), and takes it out at release() or close(), the station's stop in order. A marker left behind by a run that did not stop in order gives the file a new epoch at the next open, before any seq goes out (tests/test_outbox_epoch.py). Released, batch() hands out nothing until resume(); add() still queues. A stop in order keeps the epoch. The markers are counted here, never shown: each holds its opener's random token.",
